			"updated": 1787584859578,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "What is TTL (Time to Live):",
			"rawText": "What is TTL (Time to Live):",
			"fontSize": 28,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "What is TTL (Time to Live):",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "CFPtDYte",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 89.97468785503753,
			"y": 1766.838992983059,
			"width": 853.099365234375,
			"height": 175,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1971c2",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0S",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 553844295,
			"version": 609,
			"versionNonce": 1773854919,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": null,
			"updated": 1787585230038,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "-> TTL helps to detect the no. of hops we take to go from source to destination.\n-> With each hop the TTL decreases by 1.\n-> Whenever TTL becomes 0 router detects that this message has either stuck in\ninfinite loop on internet or has initial TTL very low that it cant reach the destination.\n-> As TTL becomes 0 the Router will drop the message and sends a ICMP error with \nmessage (Time to Live Exceeded) back to source.\n-> So source again send the message with some incremented TTL. ",
			"rawText": "-> TTL helps to detect the no. of hops we take to go from source to destination.\n-> With each hop the TTL decreases by 1.\n-> Whenever TTL becomes 0 router detects that this message has either stuck in\ninfinite loop on internet or has initial TTL very low that it cant reach the destination.\n-> As TTL becomes 0 the Router will drop the message and sends a ICMP error with \nmessage (Time to Live Exceeded) back to source.\n-> So source again send the message with some incremented TTL. ",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "-> TTL helps to detect the no. of hops we take to go from source to destination.\n-> With each hop the TTL decreases by 1.\n-> Whenever TTL becomes 0 router detects that this message has either stuck in\ninfinite loop on internet or has initial TTL very low that it cant reach the destination.\n-> As TTL becomes 0 the Router will drop the message and sends a ICMP error with \nmessage (Time to Live Exceeded) back to source.\n-> So source again send the message with some incremented TTL. ",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
